IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa29-sch2-part3`

-- coa29-tests-sch2-part3.l4: tests for coa29-sch2-part3.l4 (Schedule 2, Part 3: overseas regulatory bodies).
-- Generated by work/gen_tests_sch2p3.py. Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the Part, beside the case.


§§ `Para 1(2): relevant functions`

-- Relevant functions are functions of a public nature that appear to the Panel to be similar to its own functions, or to those of the FCA or the PRA, or to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England.
-- public; appear similar to the Panel's own functions
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 3 para 1(2) the functions are relevant functions` WITH `the functions are functions of a public nature` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority` IS FALSE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- public; appear similar to the FCA's or the PRA's
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 3 para 1(2) the functions are relevant functions` WITH `the functions are functions of a public nature` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions` IS FALSE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- public; appear similar to the Bank of England's regulatory functions
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 3 para 1(2) the functions are relevant functions` WITH `the functions are functions of a public nature` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions` IS FALSE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority` IS FALSE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- public; do not appear similar to any of them
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 3 para 1(2) the functions are relevant functions` WITH `the functions are functions of a public nature` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions` IS FALSE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority` IS FALSE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not of a public nature, although they appear similar
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 3 para 1(2) the functions are relevant functions` WITH `the functions are functions of a public nature` IS FALSE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Para 1(1): a disclosure made in accordance with this Part`

-- A disclosure is made in accordance with this Part if (a) it is made to a person or body exercising relevant functions under legislation outside the British Islands, and (b) for the purpose of enabling or assisting them to exercise those functions.
-- both limbs: relevant functions, made to assist them
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 3 para 1(1) the disclosure is made in accordance with this Part` WITH `the disclosure is made to a person or body exercising functions under legislation in a country or territory outside the British Islands` IS TRUE, `the functions are functions of a public nature` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority` IS FALSE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England` IS FALSE, `the disclosure is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting that person or body to exercise those functions` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- limb (b) fails: not made to enable or assist them
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 3 para 1(1) the disclosure is made in accordance with this Part` WITH `the disclosure is made to a person or body exercising functions under legislation in a country or territory outside the British Islands` IS TRUE, `the functions are functions of a public nature` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority` IS FALSE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England` IS FALSE, `the disclosure is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting that person or body to exercise those functions` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- limb (a) fails: functions that are not relevant functions
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 3 para 1(1) the disclosure is made in accordance with this Part` WITH `the disclosure is made to a person or body exercising functions under legislation in a country or territory outside the British Islands` IS TRUE, `the functions are functions of a public nature` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions` IS FALSE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority` IS FALSE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England` IS FALSE, `the disclosure is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting that person or body to exercise those functions` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- limb (a) fails: not a person or body exercising functions under legislation outside the British Islands
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 3 para 1(1) the disclosure is made in accordance with this Part` WITH `the disclosure is made to a person or body exercising functions under legislation in a country or territory outside the British Islands` IS FALSE, `the functions are functions of a public nature` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions` IS TRUE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority` IS FALSE, `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England` IS FALSE, `the disclosure is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting that person or body to exercise those functions` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Para 2: the Panel must have regard to the considerations`

-- In determining whether to disclose, the Panel must have regard to (a) whether the use is sufficiently important and (b) whether the person or body has adequate arrangements.
-- determining; had regard to both
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 3 para 2 the Panel has had regard to the considerations` WITH `the Panel is determining whether to disclose information to a person or body in accordance with this Part` IS TRUE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the use that the person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure` IS TRUE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the person or body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed otherwise than for the purposes of carrying out the functions mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a) or for other purposes substantially similar to those for which information disclosed to the Panel could be used or further disclosed` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- determining; (b) not had regard to (a bare 'must' not done: fork)
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 3 para 2 the Panel has had regard to the considerations` WITH `the Panel is determining whether to disclose information to a person or body in accordance with this Part` IS TRUE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the use that the person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure` IS TRUE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the person or body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed otherwise than for the purposes of carrying out the functions mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a) or for other purposes substantially similar to those for which information disclosed to the Panel could be used or further disclosed` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- determining; (a) not had regard to (a bare 'must' not done: fork)
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 3 para 2 the Panel has had regard to the considerations` WITH `the Panel is determining whether to disclose information to a person or body in accordance with this Part` IS TRUE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the use that the person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure` IS FALSE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the person or body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed otherwise than for the purposes of carrying out the functions mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a) or for other purposes substantially similar to those for which information disclosed to the Panel could be used or further disclosed` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- determining; neither (a bare 'must' not done: fork)
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 3 para 2 the Panel has had regard to the considerations` WITH `the Panel is determining whether to disclose information to a person or body in accordance with this Part` IS TRUE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the use that the person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure` IS FALSE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the person or body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed otherwise than for the purposes of carrying out the functions mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a) or for other purposes substantially similar to those for which information disclosed to the Panel could be used or further disclosed` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not determining whether to disclose under this Part: the duty is limited to that determination
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 3 para 2 the Panel has had regard to the considerations` WITH `the Panel is determining whether to disclose information to a person or body in accordance with this Part` IS FALSE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the use that the person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure` IS TRUE, `the Panel has had regard to whether the person or body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed otherwise than for the purposes of carrying out the functions mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a) or for other purposes substantially similar to those for which information disclosed to the Panel could be used or further disclosed` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

